issue.body:
If you have both `wrap-iife` and `no-extra-parens` rules turned on, then the following code:

``` javascript
var foo = (function() {
})();
```

 will throw an error `Gratuitous parentheses around expression  no-extra-parens` but the code 

``` javascript
var foo = function() {
}();
```

will throw an error `Wrap an immediate function invocation in parentheses  wrap-iife`.
